Do not double-encode array attribute values in HtmlBuilder::attributeElement().

winter/storm 1.2.15 removed its e() override (wintercms/storm#267), so e() now
double-encodes like Laravel's. Array attribute values are already escaped with
htmlspecialchars(json_encode(...)) before passing through e(), which turns
`data` passed to Form::ajax() into `&amp;quot;...`. The AJAX framework can't
parse that, so `_relation_field` / `manage_id` are dropped and relation pivot
updates (team division active toggle, playoff seeds) stop working.

Mirrors upstream commit 42e0d5b, which made the same fix for dropdown labels.

diff --git a/src/Html/HtmlBuilder.php b/src/Html/HtmlBuilder.php
--- a/src/Html/HtmlBuilder.php
+++ b/src/Html/HtmlBuilder.php
@@ -355,7 +355,7 @@ class HtmlBuilder
             $value = substr(htmlspecialchars(json_encode($value), ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8'), 1, -1);
         }
 
-        return $key.'="'.e($value).'"';
+        return $key.'="'.e($value, false).'"';
     }
 
     /**
